  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1 Model"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Long documents strain attention: its cost grows with the square of the sequence length, so a model reading a whole book spends most of its compute comparing words that never matter to each other. We restrict each position to a window and a few global tokens, which keeps the cost linear while leaving every position reachable in two steps."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The model uses attention in three different ways:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "In windowed layers, each position attends to the positions around it, as in "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "[",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "]",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Global tokens attend to every position, and every position attends to them:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "the first token of each section;"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "a learned summary token."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Decoder layers mask out every position after the current one."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The mask is applied before the softmax."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Training proceeds in stages:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Pretraining on short sequences."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Extension to long sequences."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We ask two questions:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(a) Does the window size matter?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(b) How many global tokens are enough?"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Both questions are answered by the ablations, which vary one setting at a time and keep every other choice fixed, so each difference in the results belongs to a single change in the model."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "References"
        }
      ]
    },
